WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:09.580
Wrapping up the week on Tesla Short's Time Daily, episode 466 for May 8th, 2026.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.760
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.400
Here's what's wrapping up the week in Tesla Land.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:24.860
California regulators just disclosed the Tesla Semi's battery sizes at 822 kilowatt hours

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.800
and 548 kilowatt hours.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:34.560
A filing with the California Air Resources Board confirmed those exact capacities for the two

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:42.460
production versions of the truck. The larger 822 kilowatt hour pack lines up with the higher range

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:49.300
configuration, while the smaller 548 kilowatt hour unit supports the more affordable trim

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:56.320
now entering service. Fleets gain real numbers they can use for root planning, total cost of ownership

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.320
models and decisions on where to place charging infrastructure. This marks the first public

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.400
confirmation of the specs as customer trucks begin operating on California routes.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.300
Where zero tailpipe emissions can directly reduce freight pollution in busy corridors.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:20.800
From a manufacturing standpoint, it shows Tesla is moving past prototype stages and into the kind

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:27.580
of concrete data that lets operators scale adoption without guessing. While the Semi roll-out brings

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:33.780
tangible progress on heavy-duty electrification, another recent change has left some Canadian buyers

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:41.100
questioning value on a passenger car. Canadian Model 3 buyers have been pushing back after noticing

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:48.300
reduced specifications on the premium rear-wheel drive version. The car now charges at a maximum

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:57.340
of 175 kilowatts and comes with a shorter warranty than earlier expectations. Those adjustments were

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:02.960
not clearly flagged before orders opened, which has left some owners wondering if the Canadian

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:09.020
specification still matches the price. The hardware itself supports higher speeds,

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:14.780
according to follow-up details, yet software or thermal limits are holding it back for now.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:21.560
This creates friction in one market, even as Tesla works to refine cold weather performance in

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:27.200
next-generation cells that could eventually improve range and charging in low temperatures.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.580
Owners are asking for clearer communication on what they're actually getting,

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:39.300
especially when comparing to other markets. Customer friction in one market stands in contrast

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:46.040
to Tesla's broader push to expand beyond vehicles. Tesla is now bundling solar panels with

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:52.400
Powerwall Storage as a residential package. The offering targets households that want to reduce

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:59.100
how much power they draw from the grid during peak hours. It moves the energy business into everyday

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:04.500
home use rather than staying limited to vehicle charging or larger commercial setups.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:10.720
The package gives customers a way to store energy generated on-site and use it when rates are

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:18.020
highest, which can lower bills over time. This step shows Tesla treating home energy as a complete

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:25.180
system instead of separate products sold in isolation. It also creates recurring service opportunities

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:32.480
as more installations come online across different regions. That same focus on process efficiency

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:40.200
shows up in a quieter but potentially significant manufacturing patent. A newly published patent outlines

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:47.140
terror hurts scanning for dry electrode production lines. The approach uses non-ionizing sensors

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:55.280
to measure electrode thickness and density at 0.05 millimeter resolution while the line keeps running.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:03.520
It replaces slower and more hazardous x-ray methods, letting engineers adjust gap, shear, and load

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:10.440
in real time. Because the beam checks top and bottom surfaces separately, it provides depth data

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:17.460
that transmission x-rays cannot capture. This matters especially for newer materials like silicon

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:24.460
anodes that are sensitive to compression changes. If it scales at full speed, the system cuts scrap

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:30.460
rates, shrinks the factory space needed for quality control, and supports the higher throughput required

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:36.800
from millions of vehicles annually. The technology sits at the intersection of process, physics,

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:43.760
and capital efficiency, showing how incremental sensing gains can compound into cost advantages

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:51.200
before new cell chemistry arrives. While manufacturing refinements continue, Tesla is also refreshing

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:57.700
the look of its current passenger cars. A new marine blue color is now available on the premium

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:06.440
trims of both the Model 3 and Model Y. Fires pay an extra $1,000 for the option, and it is already

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:13.900
showing up in early US orders. The addition expands color choices without requiring changes to paint

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:20.940
processes on base models. It gives customers another distinctive finish while keeping the configurator

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:27.240
simple for lower trims. Small updates like this keep the existing line up feeling current,

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:35.260
even as attention often shifts to future products. Color updates are small signals of ongoing product

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:43.220
refinement, much like Tesla's continued brand strength. Tesla leads US brand loyalty rankings according

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:51.580
to recent S&amp;P global mobility data. 61.1% of Tesla owners returned for their next vehicle,

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:58.040
the highest rate among all brands tracked. The result reflects satisfaction with software updates,

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:05.380
access to the charging network, and strong resale values. Loyalty at this level suggests owners

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:10.880
are finding enough everyday value to stay within the ecosystem rather than switching.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:17.540
It also points to how cumulative improvements in the product from over-the-air features to

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:25.200
infrastructure build repeat business over time. Loyalty metrics reflect real-world owner experience,

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:32.420
which also shows up in how people are actually using the Cybertruck. A recent Tesla video highlights

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:39.140
the Cybertrucks on-board power outlets and bullet-resistant structure. Owners are already sharing

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:45.780
examples of using those outlets to run tools on job sites. The footage reinforces the truck's

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:52.840
design as something that goes beyond daily driving into multi-purpose work. Real-world testing has

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:59.220
drawn praise even from some long-time critics, particularly around side impact and roll-over

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:06.680
performance. As the Cybertruck story plays out in public, Tesla quietly filed updated paperwork

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:14.700
on a much older model. Before we go, keep an eye on how the Terahertz scanning approach performs once

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:20.560
it moves from patent to production lines, because that could influence cost targets for the next wave

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:27.360
of vehicles. Tomorrow, we will watch for any follow-up on Canadian Model 3 specifications and whether

